<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="005" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Durable playbook run status in sprk_playbookrun / sprk_playbooknoderun</title>
    <phase>0 Removal, prerequisites and seams</phase>
    <gate>code startable; the dev Dataverse schema step needs the owner's explicit go</gate>
    <status>blocked</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api and dataverse; modifies PlaybookOrchestrationService (.cs) on the live run path and adds Dataverse columns</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Persistence on a live execution path with a fail-safe rule (a write failure never fails the run), a REST contract that must stay byte-identical, and a schema change; high-risk in plan R4</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs and a new run-record store; does not edit IPlaybookOrchestrationService.cs (001 edits its :724 comment), PlaybookRunEndpoints.cs or Api/Agent/**</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, dataverse, fields, ai, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make playbook run status durable: PlaybookOrchestrationService writes sprk_playbookrun on start, state changes and completion and sprk_playbooknoderun per node, and GetRunStatusAsync / GetRunDetailAsync read Dataverse when the run is not in memory. First add the missing columns (owner go for the dev schema change). A write failure is logged and never fails the run; no background worker.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in the JPS playbook runtime, Dataverse Web API writes and resilient side-writes.</role>
  <goal>After a BFF restart, GET /api/ai/playbooks/runs/{runId} and /detail return the stored state for a run that was started before the restart, with the same response shape as today; the schema gaps are closed; existing run tests pass.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-13 (owner: persist runs). Today run state lives only in PlaybookOrchestrationService._activeRuns (PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs:62, registered at :139/:212, read at :422/:441/:506, removed at :607), so a status check after a restart or on another instance returns not-found. Discovery (plan.md "Dataverse schema findings"): sprk_playbookrun exists (0 rows) but lacks a correlation/idempotency id, an error code, a regarding-record lookup and a short summary; sprk_playbooknoderun lacks started/completed timestamps and a sequence. specialist-legal-agents-r1 D-A18 later adds profile-version and parent-run lookups on top (not this task). Task 030 builds the MCP tools on this and enforces the StartedByOid owner rule through sprk_triggeredby.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PlaybookRuns/PlaybookRunRecordStore.cs (writes/reads sprk_playbookrun and sprk_playbooknoderun; internal interface IPlaybookRunRecordStore in the same folder)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/PlaybookRuns/PlaybookRunPersistenceTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">scripts/dataverse/Add-PlaybookRunColumns.ps1 (idempotent schema script per the dataverse-create-schema skill)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/IPlaybookOrchestrationService.cs:692-728 (PlaybookRunStatus incl. JsonIgnore StartedByOid — the REST response shape that must not change)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/PlaybookRunEndpoints.cs:245, :283, :380, :468 (status/detail consumers; not edited)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/WorkProductRecordPersister.cs (existing BFF-side Dataverse write from the AI runtime; copy its client choice and logging)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies/>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Schema: add on sprk_playbookrun a correlation/idempotency id (string, alternate key only if the skill's rules allow it on this table), an error code (string), a regarding-record lookup (polymorphic or entity-name + id pair; choose per the skill and record the choice) and a short summary (multiline, ≤ 4,000 chars); on sprk_playbooknoderun started-on and completed-on (date-time) and a sequence (whole number). Confirm and record the existing sprk_status option values and that sprk_triggeredby targets systemuser. The dev schema change runs only after the owner's explicit go in this session; until then the script is written and reviewed but not executed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-052">Writes happen inline on the run's own execution path (start, each state change, each node, completion); no BackgroundService, queue, timer or hosted service is added.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">A persistence write failure is caught, logged with an outcome code (for example playbook_run_persist_failed) and never changes the run's outcome, its streamed events or its in-memory status; the run continues.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">GetRunStatusAsync and GetRunDetailAsync keep their signatures; they return the in-memory state when present, else the stored state, else null. The REST run routes' response bodies keep their current shape byte-for-byte for the same state (PlaybookRunStatus is unchanged; StartedByOid stays JsonIgnore and is rehydrated from sprk_triggeredby's caller oid mapping or a stored oid column — record which).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not edit IPlaybookOrchestrationService.cs (task 001 edits its :724 comment), PlaybookRunEndpoints.cs or Api/Agent/**. Register the store in the existing module that registers PlaybookOrchestrationService (grep); no new module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">The store lives under Services/Ai/ and is consumed only inside the AI module; MCP tools (task 030) reach run status only through IPlaybookOrchestrationService or a PublicContracts facade, never this store directly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Persisted summary and error text exclude document content, prompts and model output beyond the short summary the run already exposes; logs carry run id, playbook id, node id, outcome code and timing only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries (the Dataverse client seam), and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

