  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Read sprk_playbookrun and sprk_playbooknoderun metadata read-only (Dataverse MCP per dataverse-mcp-usage, or the Web API EntityDefinitions endpoint); record existing columns, sprk_status option values and the sprk_triggeredby target in notes/005-schema.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Write scripts/dataverse/Add-PlaybookRunColumns.ps1 (idempotent) for the missing columns; ask the owner for the go; run it against dev only after the go and record the result in notes/005-schema.md.</step>
    <step order="3">Add PlaybookRunRecordStore and wire PlaybookOrchestrationService to write on start, state change, per node and completion, each write guarded so a failure is logged and swallowed.</step>
    <step order="4">Make GetRunStatusAsync / GetRunDetailAsync fall back to the store when the run is not in _activeRuns.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the data-mutation tests for the acceptance criteria; run the existing playbook run and AI suites.</step>
    <step order="6">Measure the publish-size delta; run the CVE check.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the owner has not given the go for the dev schema change, STOP after step 2's script review; do not run it and do not proceed with code that needs the new columns to exist at runtime without marking the task blocked.</trigger>
    <trigger>If sprk_status's option values or sprk_triggeredby's target differ from what the run state needs (for example triggeredby is a contact lookup), STOP and escalate with the metadata.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the REST run routes (GET /api/ai/playbooks/runs/{runId}, /detail) apply no caller/owner check today, do not add one here (REST bytes frozen); record it as a found defect with /project-defer-issue-tracking and tell the main session for uac-r2 (root CLAUDE.md §8.5).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row "Long-running pattern": in-memory _activeRuns in PlaybookOrchestrationService and the existing sprk_playbookrun / sprk_playbooknoderun tables (0 rows); IJobStatusService (Services/Office/) belongs to the Office module and is not used. CAPABILITY-INDEX: no row for run persistence (grep "playbookrun" .claude/patterns/CAPABILITY-INDEX.md).</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extended: PlaybookOrchestrationService keeps ownership of run state and gains a store for the existing tables; the store is a separate class only because the service already has 8+ dependencies and the persistence must be swappable in tests at the Dataverse seam.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A status check after a BFF restart or on another instance returns 404, so a run started from Copilot (FR-05) or the Console is lost to the user; FR-13 and FR-05's "run survives a restart" acceptance fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test, dotnet publish</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">scripts/dataverse/Add-PlaybookRunColumns.ps1 (dev, after owner go)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PlaybookRuns/PlaybookRunRecordStore.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">scripts/dataverse/Add-PlaybookRunColumns.ps1</output>
