  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/005-schema.md records the existing columns, the sprk_status option values, the sprk_triggeredby target, the owner's go (date) and the script result on dev.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Starting a run writes one sprk_playbookrun row (status Running, triggered-by the caller, correlation id, regarding record when the run has one); each node writes one sprk_playbooknoderun row with sequence, started-on and completed-on; completion updates status, completed-on, summary and (on failure) the error code.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With a fresh orchestration service instance (simulated restart, _activeRuns empty), GetRunStatusAsync and GetRunDetailAsync return the stored state, and the REST status/detail responses serialise identically to the in-memory responses for the same state.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: when the store throws on every write, the run completes with the same outcome and streamed events as without persistence, and a log entry with outcome code playbook_run_persist_failed is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unknown run id (neither in memory nor stored) returns null, and the REST route still returns 404.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">StartedByOid is rehydrated for stored runs and still never appears in a REST response body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing playbook run tests and the AI unit/integration suites pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (total at or under 60 MB) and no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-13, success criterion 3. The live restart check on dev is in task 039. Ask the main session to add a CAPABILITY-INDEX row proposal to notes/capability-index-pending.md for the run record store.

    2026-11-25 execution: CODE COMPLETE, PENDING OWNER GO. Status is blocked (not completed) only because the dev schema step needs the owner's explicit go, which was not given: scripts/dataverse/Add-PlaybookRunColumns.ps1 is written, parse-checked and reviewed but NOT run against any environment. Until it runs, every Person run's two record writes fail safe (logged playbook_run_persist_failed). Unblock: owner approves running the script on dev (https://spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com) (notes/005-schema.md §2), then record the go date and result there and mark this task completed. Owner decision also needed on acceptance criterion 3 (notes/005-schema.md §4: identical except the documented differences). Issues to file: orphaned Running runs (§4 item 4, owner task 030 / FR-14) and run-record retention (§4 item 6). CAPABILITY-INDEX row proposal: notes/005-schema.md §5.
